IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`

-- Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) -- cases for the seat-neutral core (rtw-core.l4) and the dates (rtw-dates.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (REPR050, and the Regulations REPR050R2), with the
-- arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. Average weekly earnings are ILLUSTRATIVE: $2,000 a week (the published
-- figure is not deposited), so the annual equivalent is $104,000 and 208 times AWE is $416,000. Dates: Monday 26 October
-- 2026 is day 0 of the claim traces. Regulative rules are asserted with EVALTRACE ... EQUALS FULFILLED where the trace
-- ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach or with an obligation still open.

`AWE` MEANS 2000

-- Builders, so that a case changes only the facts it is about.
GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN, a2 IS A BOOLEAN, a3 IS A BOOLEAN, a4 IS A BOOLEAN, a5 IS A BOOLEAN, a6 IS A BOOLEAN, a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN, a9 IS A BOOLEAN, a10 IS A BOOLEAN, a11 IS A BOOLEAN, a12 IS A BOOLEAN, a13 IS A NUMBER
      a14 IS A `Prescribed class`
GIVETH A `Worker facts`
`a person who` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 a11 a12 a13 a14 MEANS
    `Worker facts` WITH
        `works for another person under a contract`                                              IS a1
        `is an employee under the PAYG provisions, or should be`                                  IS a2
        `is employed by the Commonwealth`                                                         IS a3
        `employs another person in the work`                                                      IS a4
        `is engaged other than for the purposes of the employer's trade, business or enterprise`  IS a5
        `the employer makes PAYG withholding payments for the person`                             IS a6
        `is a prescribed family member of the employer and lives with the employer`               IS a7
        `is a director of the body corporate that employs the person`                              IS a8
        `PAYG is withheld from the director's remuneration`                                       IS a9
        `the person's details were disclosed to the employer's insurer as s 3B(4) or (6)(b) requires` IS a10
        `is employed or engaged by a householder`                                                 IS a11
        `is under the contract a contestant in a sporting or athletic activity, or training or travelling for one` IS a12
        `yearly remuneration`                                                                     IS a13
        `prescribed class`                                                                        IS a14

GIVEN c1 IS A `Jurisdiction`, c2 IS A `Jurisdiction`, c3 IS A `Jurisdiction`, c4 IS A BOOLEAN, c5 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Connection facts`
`a connection where` c1 c2 c3 c4 c5 MEANS
    `Connection facts` WITH
        `where the worker usually works in the employment`                      IS c1
        `where the worker is usually based for the employment`                  IS c2
        `where the employer's principal place of business in Australia is`      IS c3
        `the worker was in the Territory when injured`                          IS c4
        `a place outside Australia may compensate the worker for the same matter` IS c5

GIVEN i1 IS A BOOLEAN, i2 IS A BOOLEAN, i3 IS A BOOLEAN, i4 IS A BOOLEAN, i5 IS A BOOLEAN, i6 IS A BOOLEAN, i7 IS A BOOLEAN
      i8 IS A BOOLEAN, i9 IS A BOOLEAN, i10 IS A BOOLEAN, i11 IS A BOOLEAN, i12 IS A NUMBER, i13 IS A BOOLEAN
      i14 IS A BOOLEAN, i15 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
`an injury that` i1 i2 i3 i4 i5 i6 i7 i8 i9 i10 i11 i12 i13 i14 i15 MEANS
    `Injury facts` WITH
        `arose out of or in the course of the employment`                                         IS i1
        `is a mental injury caused wholly or primarily by reasonable management action`           IS i2
        `was sustained in a motor accident that s 4(2A) takes out of the employment`               IS i3
        `resulted in or materially contributed to death, impairment or incapacity`                IS i4
        `is a heart attack or stroke injury`                                                      IS i5
        `the employment materially contributed to the heart attack or stroke`                     IS i6
        `was deliberately self-inflicted`                                                         IS i7
        `is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`                           IS i8
        `resulted in death or permanent or long-term incapacity`                                  IS i9
        `was sustained while the worker was driving a motor vehicle`                              IS i10
        `the worker had consumed alcoholic liquor`                                                IS i11
        `the worker's alcohol concentration, in grams per 100 millilitres of blood or per 210 litres of breath` IS i12
        `the consumption is found to have materially contributed to the accident`                 IS i13
        `the contrary of the s 60(2) presumption is proved`                                       IS i14
        `the worker was under the influence of a drug`                                            IS i15

-- An employee on PAYG, paid $80,000 a year, in no prescribed class.
`an ordinary employee` MEANS `a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 `in neither prescribed class`

-- Usually works in the Territory.
`a Territory job` MEANS `a connection where` `the Territory` `the Territory` `the Territory` TRUE FALSE

-- A physical injury at work that stops the worker working, with no exclusion.
`an ordinary injury` MEANS `an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Dates`

-- Monday 26 October 2026: the 3rd working day after is Thursday 29 October; the 10th is Monday 9 November (Tue 27 to
-- Fri 30 are 1-4, Mon 2 to Fri 6 November are 5-9, Mon 9 is 10). From Friday 30 October, the 3rd is Wednesday 4 November.
-- With one weekday public holiday in the period, the 3rd from Monday 26 October is Friday 30 October.
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 10 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 30 10 2026) `with public holidays` 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 4 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last of` 3 `working days after` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) `with public holidays` 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 10 2026
#ASSERT `is a Monday to Friday` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a Monday to Friday` (`the calendar date` 1 11 2026))
-- 31 August 2026 plus 6 months: 31 February 2027 does not exist, so 28 February 2027. 31 January 2028 plus 1 month is
-- 29 February 2028 (a leap year). 15 September 2026 less 6 months is 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026) `plus months` 6 EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 31 1 2028) `plus months` 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 15 9 2026) `plus months` (0 MINUS 6) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
-- Born 1 July 1960, 804 months (67 years) old on 1 July 2027.
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `attains an age in months of` 804 EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 7 2027
#ASSERT `days from` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) `to` (`the calendar date` 9 11 2026) EQUALS 14

§ `s 3B -- who is a worker`

#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` `an ordinary employee` `AWE`
-- Not a PAYG employee and not one in substance: not a worker (s 3B(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
-- Employed by the Commonwealth (s 3B(2)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
-- Engaged privately and no PAYG withholding (s 3B(2)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
-- A son living with his employer: not a worker unless disclosed to the insurer (s 3B(3), (4)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 50000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 50000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`
-- A director: a worker only if PAYG is withheld and the director is disclosed (s 3B(5), (6)).
#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 120000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 120000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
-- A householder's nanny on PAYG: reg 4A's amount is 20% of $104,000 = $20,800. $20,000 is not more: not a worker;
-- $25,000 is: a worker (s 3B(10), (11)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 20000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 25000 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`
-- A paid sports contestant: reg 5's amount is 65% of $104,000 = $67,600; "not less than" it is a worker (s 3B(14), (15)).
#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 67600 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 67599 `in neither prescribed class`) `AWE`)
-- Reg 3A(1): a taxi driver for an accredited, approved operator is a worker even off PAYG; reg 3A(2): a foster carer is
-- not, even on PAYG (s 3B(17)).
#ASSERT `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 `prescribed as a worker by reg 3A(1)`) `AWE`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a worker under s 3B` (`a person who` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40000 `prescribed as not a worker by reg 3A(2)`) `AWE`)

§ `s 53AA -- connected with the Territory`

#ASSERT `the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` `a Territory job`
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` (`a connection where` `another State or Territory` `the Territory` `the Territory` TRUE FALSE))
-- No one jurisdiction where the worker works (a fly-in fly-out roster across three), based in Darwin.
#ASSERT `the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` (`a connection where` `no one jurisdiction` `the Territory` `another State or Territory` FALSE FALSE)
-- Neither works nor is based in any one jurisdiction; the employer's ABN address is in Darwin.
#ASSERT `the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` (`a connection where` `no one jurisdiction` `no one jurisdiction` `the Territory` FALSE FALSE)
-- No jurisdiction at all (an overseas employer): in the Territory when injured, and no foreign scheme (s 53AA(3)).
#ASSERT `the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` (`a connection where` `no one jurisdiction` `no one jurisdiction` `no one jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the employment is connected with the Territory under s 53AA` (`a connection where` `no one jurisdiction` `no one jurisdiction` `no one jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE))

§ `ss 3A, 4, 53, 57, 58, 60 -- is the injury compensable`

#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` `an ordinary injury` `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` (`a person who` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 80000 `in neither prescribed class`) `a Territory job` `an ordinary injury` `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: not a worker (s 3B)`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` (`a connection where` `another State or Territory` `the Territory` `the Territory` TRUE FALSE) `an ordinary injury` `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: the employment is not connected with the Territory (ss 53(2), 53AA)`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: not an injury arising out of or in the course of the employment (ss 3A(1), 4)`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: a mental injury caused wholly or primarily by reasonable management action (s 3A(2))`
-- A car crash driving home from the usual workplace: s 4(2A)(b) leaves it to the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act.
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: a motor accident in a recess or on a journey that s 4(2A) takes out`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: no death, impairment or incapacity (s 53(1))`
-- A heart attack at work: compensable only if the work materially contributed (s 58).
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: a heart attack or stroke to which the employment did not materially contribute (s 58)`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: deliberately self-inflicted (s 57(a))`
-- Serious and wilful misconduct bars compensation only where the injury does not cause death or permanent or long-term
-- incapacity (s 57(b)).
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `not compensable: serious and wilful misconduct, and no death or permanent or long-term incapacity (s 57(b))`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
-- s 60: driving for work at 0.09, the presumption unrebutted: weekly payments and the lump sum go; death benefits,
-- medical costs and rehabilitation stay (s 60(3)). At 0.09 with the contrary proved and no finding: compensable. At 0.05
-- with a finding that it contributed: limited. Under the influence of a drug: limited.
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.09 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable only for death benefits, medical and other costs and rehabilitation (s 60(3))`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.09 FALSE TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.05 TRUE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable only for death benefits, medical and other costs and rehabilitation (s 60(3))`
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable only for death benefits, medical and other costs and rehabilitation (s 60(3))`
-- Not driving: s 60 does not reach a passenger, whatever the reading.
#ASSERT `whether the injury is compensable` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0.12 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `compensable under Part 5`
-- For the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act s 10A(b).
#ASSERT `the injury would be compensable but for s 57` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` (`an injury that` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE`
#ASSERT NOT (`the injury would be compensable but for s 57` `an ordinary employee` `a Territory job` `an ordinary injury` `AWE`)
#ASSERT `the answer allows weekly payments and the impairment lump sum` `compensable under Part 5`
#ASSERT NOT (`the answer allows weekly payments and the impairment lump sum` `compensable only for death benefits, medical and other costs and rehabilitation (s 60(3))`)

§ `ss 82, 182 and reg 12 -- notice, claim and certificate`

-- Injury 1 March 2026: the 6 months end on 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to claim under s 182(1)` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 9 2026

GIVEN `claimed on` IS A DATE, `notice before leaving` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice excused` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `employer conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claim time facts`
`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` `claimed on` `notice before leaving` `notice excused` `reasonable cause` `employer conduct` MEANS
    `Claim time facts` WITH
        `the day of the injury, or of the incapacity from a disease, or the day advice of the death was received` IS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
        `the day the claim was made`                                                    IS `claimed on`
        `notice of the injury was given before the worker voluntarily left the employment` IS `notice before leaving`
        `the employer is not prejudiced, or the want of notice had a reasonable cause`   IS `notice excused`
        `the late claim is found to have been occasioned by mistake, ignorance of a disease, absence from the Territory or other reasonable cause` IS `reasonable cause`
        `the claimant was paid what they believed was compensation, or the employer or insurer led them to believe compensation would be paid or was not available` IS `employer conduct`

#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `maintainable: notice given and the claim made within 6 months (s 182(1))`
#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not maintainable: the claim was not made within 6 months and no reasonable cause is found (s 182(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `maintainable: the want of notice or the late claim is excused (s 182(2), (3), (5))`
-- The insurer's adjuster told the worker the claim would be paid: a reasonable cause by s 182(5)(b).
#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `maintainable: the want of notice or the late claim is excused (s 182(2), (3), (5))`
#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not maintainable: no notice before the worker voluntarily left the employment, and s 182(2) does not excuse it`
#ASSERT `whether proceedings on the claim are maintainable under s 182` (`a claim for a 1 March 2026 injury made on` (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `maintainable: the want of notice or the late claim is excused (s 182(2), (3), (5))`
-- s 82(2): first document on 1 October 2026, the second by 29 October 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to give the remaining claim document under s 82(2)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026
-- Reg 12(2): a doctor's certificate of 1 October 2026 has effect to 15 October; a remote nurse's, without consulting a
-- doctor, to 4 October. Both lapse well inside the 28 days s 82(2) allows for the claim form (finding 13).
#ASSERT `the last day a certificate has effect` `a medical practitioner` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day a certificate has effect` `a prescribed person who did not consult a medical practitioner` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 4 10 2026
#ASSERT `the days a medical certificate of capacity has effect under reg 12(2)` `a prescribed person who consulted a medical practitioner` EQUALS 14

§ `s 49A -- normal weekly earnings`

GIVEN `in kind` IS A NUMBER, `fly in fly out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
`earnings with` `in kind` `fly in fly out` MEANS
    `Earnings facts` WITH
        `weekly ordinary remuneration from the employer liable to compensate`               IS 1500
        `weekly ordinary remuneration from other employers the worker ordinarily works for` IS 300
        `weekly wages for overtime worked in a regular and established pattern`             IS 200
        `weekly over-award payments`                                                        IS 50
        `weekly climate, district, leading hand, qualification or regular shift allowances and service grants` IS 100
        `weekly value of electricity, meals or accommodation provided other than in money`  IS `in kind`
        `is a fly-in fly-out or drive-in drive-out worker`                                  IS `fly in fly out`

-- $1,500 + $300 + $200 + $50 + $100 = $2,150, plus accommodation worth $900 capped at 35% of $2,000 = $700: $2,850.
-- A fly-in fly-out worker's accommodation is not counted: $2,150. Accommodation worth $400 is under the cap: $2,550.
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings under s 49A` (`earnings with` 900 FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS 2850
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings under s 49A` (`earnings with` 900 TRUE) `AWE` EQUALS 2150
#ASSERT `the normal weekly earnings under s 49A` (`earnings with` 400 FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS 2550

§ `ss 64, 65 -- the weekly amount`

-- s 64(3): $1,800 less $600 earned = $1,200; earning $2,000 leaves nothing.
#ASSERT `the s 64 weekly amount` 1800 600 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the s 64 weekly amount` 1800 2000 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `indexed` IS A NUMBER, `capable` IS A NUMBER, `spouse dependent` IS A BOOLEAN, `children` IS A NUMBER, `spouse earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Long-term incapacity facts`
`long-term facts with` `indexed` `capable` `spouse dependent` `children` `spouse earnings` MEANS
    `Long-term incapacity facts` WITH
        `indexed normal weekly earnings`                                   IS `indexed`
        `the amount the worker is reasonably capable of earning in a week`  IS `capable`
        `the worker's spouse is wholly or mainly dependent on the worker`   IS `spouse dependent`
        `the number of the worker's prescribed children`                    IS `children`
        `the worker's spouse's normal weekly earnings`                      IS `spouse earnings`

-- Partial: indexed $1,900, capable of $700, loss $1,200; 75% is $900, under 150% of $2,000 = $3,000. The (8) floor: 75% of
-- $1,900 = $1,425 is not less than the (12) amount of 50% of $2,000 = $1,000. $900.
#ASSERT `the loss of earning capacity under s 65(2)` (`long-term facts with` 1900 700 FALSE 0 0) EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1900 700 FALSE 0 0) `AWE` EQUALS 900
-- Total, a high earner: indexed $5,000, loss $5,000, 75% is $3,750, capped at $3,000.
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 5000 0 FALSE 0 0) `AWE` EQUALS 3000
-- Total, a low earner with a dependent spouse and two prescribed children: indexed $1,200, loss $1,200, (1B) $900. The
-- (12) amount is $2,000 x (50% + 12.5% + 2 x 6.25%) = $1,500. $900 is less, so (7): the lesser of 90% of $1,200 = $1,080
-- and $1,500. $1,080.
#ASSERT `the s 65(12) amount` (`long-term facts with` 1200 0 TRUE 2 0) `AWE` EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1200 0 TRUE 2 0) `AWE` EQUALS 1080
-- The same, but the spouse earns $3,000 a week, which is 150% of $2,000: (10) shuts out the floor. $900.
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1200 0 TRUE 2 3000) `AWE` EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1200 0 TRUE 2 2999) `AWE` EQUALS 1080
-- Partial, a low earner: indexed $1,200, capable of $400, loss $800, (1B) $600. (8): 75% of $1,200 = $900 is less than
-- $1,500; (9): $1,500 / $1,200 = 125% of the loss = $1,000; 90% of the loss = $720. The lesser: $720.
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1200 400 TRUE 2 0) `AWE` EQUALS 720
-- Partial, where the (9) percentage is under 90%: indexed $1,300, capable of $300, loss $1,000, (1B) $750. (12) with one
-- prescribed child: $2,000 x 56.25% = $1,125. 75% of $1,300 = $975 is less, so (8): the lesser of $900 and
-- $1,125 / $1,300 x $1,000 = $865.38 (exactly 11250/13).
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 1300 300 FALSE 1 0) `AWE` EQUALS (11250 DIVIDED BY 13)
-- Total, not a low earner: indexed $2,000, (1B) $1,500, not less than the (12) amount of $1,000. $1,500.
#ASSERT `the s 65 weekly amount` (`long-term facts with` 2000 0 FALSE 0 0) `AWE` EQUALS 1500
-- FLAGGED READING of s 65(3A): $1,500 x $2,100 / $2,000 = $1,575.
#ASSERT `the indexed normal weekly earnings on the flagged reading N x A / C` 1500 2100 2000 EQUALS 1575

GIVEN `weeks paid` IS A NUMBER, `certified` IS A BOOLEAN, `fifteen or more` IS A BOOLEAN, `prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN, `abroad` IS A BOOLEAN, `declarations` IS A BOOLEAN, `court extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Week facts`
`a week after` `weeks paid` `certified` `fifteen or more` `prisoner` `abroad` `declarations` `court extension` MEANS
    `Week facts` WITH
        `the weeks of weekly payments already paid for the injury`                         IS `weeks paid`
        `a medical practitioner certifies the worker incapacitated for the week`           IS `certified`
        `the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more`                        IS `fifteen or more`
        `normal weekly earnings`                                                           IS 1800
        `the amount the worker actually earned in employment during the week`              IS 0
        `the worker is a prisoner, or detained outside the Territory, and someone is liable to maintain the worker` IS `prisoner`
        `the worker lives outside Australia`                                               IS `abroad`
        `the worker gives the reg 6A declarations`                                         IS `declarations`
        `the employer is satisfied about the worker's continued incapacity`                IS `declarations`
        `a Court order under s 65B(4) extends the entitlement for the week`                IS `court extension`
        `the weeks after the first 26 already paid while the worker lived outside Australia` IS 0
        `long-term facts`                                                                  IS `long-term facts with` 1900 700 FALSE 0 0

-- The same week, for a worker living outside Australia who has the declarations and the employer's satisfaction, with
-- the weeks already paid and how many of those after the 26th were paid while abroad.
GIVEN `weeks paid` IS A NUMBER, `weeks abroad after the 26th` IS A NUMBER, `declarations` IS A BOOLEAN, `court extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Week facts`
`a week abroad after` `weeks paid` `of which abroad after the 26th` `weeks abroad after the 26th` `declarations` `court extension` MEANS
    `Week facts` WITH
        `the weeks of weekly payments already paid for the injury`                         IS `weeks paid`
        `a medical practitioner certifies the worker incapacitated for the week`           IS FALSE
        `the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more`                        IS FALSE
        `normal weekly earnings`                                                           IS 1800
        `the amount the worker actually earned in employment during the week`              IS 0
        `the worker is a prisoner, or detained outside the Territory, and someone is liable to maintain the worker` IS FALSE
        `the worker lives outside Australia`                                               IS TRUE
        `the worker gives the reg 6A declarations`                                         IS `declarations`
        `the employer is satisfied about the worker's continued incapacity`                IS `declarations`
        `a Court order under s 65B(4) extends the entitlement for the week`                IS `court extension`
        `the weeks after the first 26 already paid while the worker lived outside Australia` IS `weeks abroad after the 26th`
        `long-term facts`                                                                  IS `long-term facts with` 1900 700 FALSE 0 0

-- The first week, certified, nothing earned: $1,800 under s 64. The 26th week (25 paid): still s 64. The 27th (26 paid):
-- s 65, $900 as above.
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 64 compensation, in dollars for the week` 1800
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 25 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 64 compensation, in dollars for the week` 1800
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 26 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: the week is not certified by a medical practitioner (s 64(2), (5)(b))`
-- After 260 weeks: nothing under 15%; at 15% or more the 260 weeks do not apply.
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 260 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: the 260 weeks have been paid (ss 65(1BA), 61A(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 259 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 400 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week after` 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: suspended while a prisoner (s 65A)`
-- Living abroad (s 65B, on the reading of finding 19). Abroad since week 27, 50 weeks paid (24 of them abroad): without
-- the declarations, suspended; with them, 26 + 24 = 50 weeks count, under 104, so paid $900. 104 weeks paid, 78 of them
-- abroad: 26 + 78 = 104 count, so the continued entitlement has ceased, unless a Court extension covers the week.
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 50 `of which abroad after the 26th` 24 FALSE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: suspended while living outside Australia (s 65B)`
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 50 `of which abroad after the 26th` 24 TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 104 `of which abroad after the 26th` 78 TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: suspended while living outside Australia (s 65B)`
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 104 `of which abroad after the 26th` 78 TRUE TRUE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
-- Paid 104 weeks in the Territory, then moved abroad: only the first 26 count, so paid $900 (the first version said
-- suspended). 181 weeks paid, 77 abroad: 26 + 77 = 103, paid; 182 paid, 78 abroad: 104, ceased.
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 104 `of which abroad after the 26th` 0 TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 181 `of which abroad after the 26th` 77 TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `s 65 compensation, in dollars for the week` 900
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for the week` (`a week abroad after` 182 `of which abroad after the 26th` 78 TRUE FALSE) `AWE` EQUALS `none: suspended while living outside Australia (s 65B)`

§ `s 65(1D) -- until when`

GIVEN `born` IS A DATE, `injured` IS A DATE, `pension months` IS A NUMBER, `retiring months` IS A NUMBER, `fifteen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period facts`
`a worker born` `born` `injured on` `injured` `with pension age` `pension months` `and retiring age` `retiring months` `at 15% or more` `fifteen` MEANS
    `Period facts` WITH
        `the worker's date of birth`                                          IS `born`
        `the injury date`                                                     IS `injured`
        `the worker's future pension age, in months`                          IS `pension months`
        `the normal retiring age in the worker's industry or occupation, in months` IS `retiring months`
        `the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more`           IS `fifteen`

-- Born 1 July 1980: pension age 67 (804 months) on 1 July 2047. Injured 1 March 2026, long before.
-- (a)(ii): 15% or more, retiring age 65 (780) not later: until 1 July 2047.
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1980) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 780 `at 15% or more` TRUE) EQUALS `until the worker attains future pension age, on` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2047)
-- (b)(ii): under 15%: 260 weeks, or 1 July 2047 if earlier.
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1980) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 780 `at 15% or more` FALSE) EQUALS `until 260 weeks have been paid, or future pension age on this day if that is earlier` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2047)
-- (a)(i), (b)(i): retiring age 68 (816), later: 1 July 2048.
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1980) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 816 `at 15% or more` TRUE) EQUALS `until the worker attains normal retiring age, on` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2048)
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1980) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 816 `at 15% or more` FALSE) EQUALS `until 260 weeks have been paid, or normal retiring age on this day if that is earlier` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2048)
-- Exactly 2 years before pension age: born 1 July 1960 (pension age 1 July 2027), injured 1 July 2025: (a)(ii).
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2025) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 780 `at 15% or more` TRUE) EQUALS `until the worker attains future pension age, on` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2027)
-- (c)(iii): the same worker injured 1 March 2026, less than 2 years before 1 July 2027: 104 weeks (728 days) from the
-- injury date, to 27 February 2028 (1 March 2026 plus 365 is 1 March 2027, plus 363 more, across 29 February 2028).
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 780 `at 15% or more` TRUE) EQUALS `for 104 weeks from the injury date, to` (`the calendar date` 27 2 2028)
-- (c)(iv): born 1 July 1955, pension age 66 and 6 months (798) on 1 January 2022; injured after it, 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1955) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 798 `and retiring age` 780 `at 15% or more` FALSE) EQUALS `for 104 weeks from the injury date, to` (`the calendar date` 27 2 2028)
-- (c)(i): born 1 July 1960, retiring age 68 (816) on 1 July 2028, later than pension age; injured 1 March 2027, less than
-- 2 years before it: 104 weeks to 26 February 2029.
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2027) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 816 `at 15% or more` FALSE) EQUALS `for 104 weeks from the injury date, to` (`the calendar date` 26 2 2029)
-- GAP (finding 3): born 1 July 1960, pension age 1 July 2027, retiring age 70 (840) on 1 July 2030; injured 1 March 2026:
-- less than 2 years before pension age, so not (a) or (b); 2 years or more before retiring age, so not (c)(i) or (ii);
-- retiring age is later, so not (c)(iii) or (iv).
#ASSERT `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)` (`a worker born` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) `injured on` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `with pension age` 804 `and retiring age` 840 `at 15% or more` TRUE) EQUALS `not covered: s 65(1D) states no period for an injury less than 2 years before future pension age but 2 years or more before a later normal retiring age`

-- s 61A(2)(a)(ii): the 260th week ends 30 June 2031; costs incurred to 30 June 2032 can be paid.
#ASSERT `the last day a cost may be incurred under s 61A(2)(a)(ii)` (`the calendar date` 30 6 2031) EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 6 2032
-- s 61B(4): a notice posted 1 October 2026 for an event on 10 October takes effect 15 October (14 days after notice); a
-- notice of 1 September takes effect on the event day, 10 October.
#ASSERT `the day the change takes effect under s 61B(4)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the change takes effect under s 61B(4)` (`the calendar date` 1 9 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 10 10 2026

§ `ss 70-72 -- permanent impairment`

-- 208 x $2,000 = $416,000. Below 5%: none. 5% to under 10%: 2% = $8,320. 10%: 3% = $12,480. 11%: 4% = $16,640. 12%: 6%
-- = $24,960. 13%: 8% = $33,280. 14%: 12% = $49,920. 15%: 15% = $62,400. 30%: $124,800. 84%: $349,440. 85% and above:
-- $416,000. 14.5%: no row.
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 4 `AWE` EQUALS `none: less than 5% of the whole person is not a permanent impairment (s 70)`
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 5 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 8320
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 9.5 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 8320
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 10 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 12480
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 11 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 16640
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 12 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 24960
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 13 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 33280
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 14 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 49920
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 14.5 `AWE` EQUALS `not covered: the Table to s 71(3) has no row for a percentage from 10% to 15% that is not a whole number`
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 15 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 62400
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 30 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 124800
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 84 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 349440
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 85 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 416000
#ASSERT `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` 100 `AWE` EQUALS `a lump sum, in dollars, of` 416000
-- Notified of the assessment 1 October 2026: a reassessment by 29 October; with none, payment by 12 November. Notified of
-- a reassessment 1 December 2026: payment by 29 December.
#ASSERT `the last day to apply for a reassessment under s 72(3)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to pay under s 71(4)(a)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 12 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to pay under s 71(4)(b)` (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 12 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the permanent impairment compensation under s 71(4)` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 12 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the permanent impairment compensation under s 71(4)` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 12 2026

§ `ss 62, 63 -- death`

-- Reg 6: 20% of $104,000 = $20,800. A $15,000 funeral: $15,000; a $25,000 funeral: $20,800.
#ASSERT `the funeral benefit under s 62(1)(a)` 15000 `AWE` EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT `the funeral benefit under s 62(1)(a)` 25000 `AWE` EQUALS 20800

GIVEN `spouse` IS A BOOLEAN, `children` IS A NUMBER, `others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dependants`
`dependants` `spouse` `children` `others` MEANS
    `Dependants` WITH
        `there is a dependant spouse`      IS `spouse`
        `the number of dependant children` IS `children`
        `there are other dependants`       IS `others`

-- 364 x $2,000 = $728,000.
#ASSERT `the s 62(1)(b) amount` `AWE` EQUALS 728000
-- Spouse alone: $728,000; no child's share.
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 0 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 728000
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 0 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `no share: there is no dependant of that kind`
-- Spouse and one child: 10% = $72,800 to the child, $655,200 to the spouse.
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 1 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 655200
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 1 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 72800
-- Spouse and two children: 5% = $36,400 each, $655,200 to the spouse: the children together get the same 10% as one
-- child alone (finding 10).
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 2 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 36400
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 2 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 655200
-- Spouse and five children: 5% each, 75% = $546,000 to the spouse. Six: 25% shared, $182,000 / 6 each; the spouse $546,000.
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 5 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 546000
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 6 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` (91000 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 6 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 546000
-- No spouse: one child takes $728,000; three share it equally.
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` FALSE 1 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` 728000
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`each child's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` FALSE 3 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `a share, in dollars, of` (728000 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` FALSE 3 FALSE)) `AWE` EQUALS `no share: there is no dependant of that kind`
-- A dependent parent as well: the Court decides (s 62(1)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `the death share from` (`the spouse's proportion under the s 62(3) Table` (`dependants` TRUE 1 TRUE)) `AWE` EQUALS `as the Court determines on an application under s 62(2)`
-- s 62(4): a 12-year-old's share goes to the Public Trustee; a 19-year-old's does not; nor where the Court orders otherwise.
#ASSERT `the child's share is paid to the Public Trustee under s 62(4)` 12 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the child's share is paid to the Public Trustee under s 62(4)` 19 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the child's share is paid to the Public Trustee under s 62(4)` 12 TRUE)
-- s 62(1)(c): no amount is prescribed, so $3,000 of reasonable costs is paid in full; under a cap of $2,000, $2,000.
#ASSERT `the counselling and financial advice costs payable under s 62(1)(c)` 3000 NOTHING EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the counselling and financial advice costs payable under s 62(1)(c)` 3000 (JUST 2000) EQUALS 2000
-- s 63: 10% of $2,000 = $200 a week for each of three children, or ten. Twelve share 100%: $2,000 / 12 each.
#ASSERT `the weekly benefit for each prescribed child under s 63` 3 `AWE` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the weekly benefit for each prescribed child under s 63` 10 `AWE` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the weekly benefit for each prescribed child under s 63` 12 `AWE` EQUALS (500 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `the weekly benefit for each prescribed child under s 63` 0 `AWE` EQUALS 0

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `student` IS A BOOLEAN, `married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Child facts`
`a child aged` `age` `student` `married` MEANS
    `Child facts` WITH
        `is a child of the worker or one the worker stood in loco parentis to` IS TRUE
        `age in years`                                                       IS `age`
        `is a full-time student, or physically or mentally handicapped`       IS `student`
        `is the spouse of another person`                                    IS `married`

#ASSERT `the child is a prescribed child under ss 63(3) and 65(13)` (`a child aged` 15 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the child is a prescribed child under ss 63(3) and 65(13)` (`a child aged` 18 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the child is a prescribed child under ss 63(3) and 65(13)` (`a child aged` 18 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the child is a prescribed child under ss 63(3) and 65(13)` (`a child aged` 21 TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the child is a prescribed child under ss 63(3) and 65(13)` (`a child aged` 17 FALSE TRUE))

§ `s 74 -- overpayments`

#ASSERT `whether the overpayment can be recovered under s 74` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not recoverable unless the Court orders otherwise: the employer or insurer calculated the benefit incorrectly (s 74(2)(a))`
-- Recovery sought 1 August 2026; 6 months before is 1 February 2026. A period ending 1 January 2026 is more than 6 months
-- before; one ending 1 March 2026 is not; one ending 1 February 2026 is exactly 6 months before, not more.
#ASSERT `whether the overpayment can be recovered under s 74` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not recoverable unless the Court orders otherwise: it was paid for a period more than 6 months before recovery was sought (s 74(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `whether the overpayment can be recovered under s 74` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `the overpayment may be recovered from the worker`
#ASSERT `whether the overpayment can be recovered under s 74` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 2 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `the overpayment may be recovered from the worker`

§ `ss 84-89 -- the employer's deadlines`

-- Claim received Monday 26 October 2026: forward by Thursday 29 October; decide by Monday 9 November. Accepted or
-- deferred Wednesday 4 November: payments by Monday 9 November. Deferral notified 4 November: in force to 30 December
-- (56 days). A request for earnings information received 1 October: by 22 October. An application to alter payments
-- received 1 October: by 15 October. The week ending Sunday 1 November: paid by Sunday 8 November.
#ASSERT `the last day to forward the claim under s 84(1)` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to notify a decision under s 85(1)` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to commence weekly payments under s 85(2) or (4)(b)` (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of a deferral under s 85(4)(a)` (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 12 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to give earnings information under s 85A(2)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 22 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to decide an application to alter weekly payments under s 86(2)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to make the weekly payment under s 88(1)` (`the calendar date` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 8 11 2026
#ASSERT `where the claim must be forwarded under s 84(1)` `uninsured` EQUALS `forward the claim to the Nominal Insurer and a copy to the Authority, and keep a copy (s 84(1)(ab), (c))`
#ASSERT `where the claim must be forwarded under s 84(1)` `insured with an approved insurer` EQUALS `forward the claim, and a copy, to the insurer, and keep a copy (s 84(1)(b), (c))`

GIVEN `notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified on` IS A DATE, `decision` IS A `Liability decision`, `final` IS A BOOLEAN, `final on` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Decision facts`
`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` `notified` `notified on` `decision` `final` `final on` `today` MEANS
    `Decision facts` WITH
        `the day the employer received the claim`                         IS `the calendar date` 26 10 2026
        `weekday public holidays in the 10 working days`                  IS 0
        `the employer has notified a decision`                            IS `notified`
        `the day the decision was notified or posted`                     IS `notified on`
        `the decision`                                                    IS `decision`
        `after deferring, the employer has notified acceptance or a dispute` IS `final`
        `the day that later decision was notified or posted`              IS `final on`
        `today`                                                           IS `today`

-- Accepted on 5 November, inside the 10 working days to 9 November: not deemed.
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) `accept liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026)) EQUALS `not deemed: the employer notified a decision in time`
-- No decision yet on 6 November: not yet, until 9 November. Still none on 10 November: deemed accepted (s 87(1)).
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` FALSE (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) `accept liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026)) EQUALS `not yet: the employer may still notify a decision, until` (`the calendar date` 9 11 2026)
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` FALSE (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) `accept liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026)) EQUALS `deemed accepted under s 87(1): no decision was notified within 10 working days`
-- A dispute notified on 5 November without the s 85(8) statement is still a decision notified within the 10 working days
-- to 9 November: s 87(1) turns on that, and s 87(3) speaks only "for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) or (2)(a)". So
-- not deemed, with s 85(8) unmet (finding 18; corrected 24 October 2026 from "deemed accepted").
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement` FALSE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026)) EQUALS `not deemed: the employer notified a dispute in time, but without the s 85(8) statement, so it has not met s 85(8)`
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) `dispute liability, with the s 85(8) statement` FALSE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026)) EQUALS `not deemed: the employer notified a decision in time`
-- Deferred on 4 November: in force to 30 December. On 1 December, not yet; on 31 December with no decision, deemed
-- accepted (s 87(2)); a decision to accept or dispute (with the statement or without it, s 85(4)(a)) on 20 December ends
-- it in time.
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) `defer accepting liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026)) EQUALS `not yet: the deferral is in force, until` (`the calendar date` 30 12 2026)
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) `defer accepting liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 12 2026)) EQUALS `deemed accepted under s 87(2): the deferral ran out without a decision`
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 4 11 2026) `defer accepting liability` TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 12 2026)) EQUALS `not deemed: the employer notified a decision in time`
-- A deferral notified on 10 November is too late to count: deemed accepted under s 87(1).
#ASSERT `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87` (`a claim received 26 October 2026 with` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026) `defer accepting liability` FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 11 11 2026)) EQUALS `deemed accepted under s 87(1): no decision was notified within 10 working days`
-- Deemed accepted from Tuesday 10 November; the employer notifies a decision on Friday 20 November. Acceptance, or a
-- dispute with the s 85(8) statement: the deemed acceptance runs until the expiry of 14 days after, 4 December (s 87(1)(a)).
-- A dispute without the statement is not a notification for (1)(a) (s 87(3)(b)), so it does not end it. A deferral: not
-- covered.
#ASSERT `when a deemed acceptance ends under s 87(1)(a), (2)(a) and (3)` `accept liability` (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `the deemed acceptance runs until the expiry of 14 days after the notice, to` (`the calendar date` 4 12 2026)
#ASSERT `when a deemed acceptance ends under s 87(1)(a), (2)(a) and (3)` `dispute liability, with the s 85(8) statement` (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `the deemed acceptance runs until the expiry of 14 days after the notice, to` (`the calendar date` 4 12 2026)
#ASSERT `when a deemed acceptance ends under s 87(1)(a), (2)(a) and (3)` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement` (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `not ended by this notice: a dispute without the s 85(8) statement is not a notification for s 87(1)(a) and (2)(a) (s 87(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `when a deemed acceptance ends under s 87(1)(a), (2)(a) and (3)` `defer accepting liability` (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `not covered: whether a notice of deferral ends a deemed acceptance (s 87(1)(a), (2)(a))`
-- READING (finding 12): on the deemed acceptance, weekly payments by the 3rd working day after Tuesday 10 November, the
-- day acceptance is deemed: Wednesday 11, Thursday 12, Friday 13 November. With one weekday public holiday in those
-- days, Monday 16 November.
#ASSERT `the last day to commence weekly payments on a deemed acceptance under s 87(1), on the s 85(2) reading` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) 0 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 13 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to commence weekly payments on a deemed acceptance under s 87(1), on the s 85(2) reading` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) 0 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 16 11 2026

GIVEN `reasons` IS A BOOLEAN, `bulletin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dispute statement facts`
`a dispute statement with` `reasons` `bulletin` MEANS
    `Dispute statement facts` WITH
        `is in the approved form`                                                             IS TRUE
        `sets out the reasons in enough detail for the claimant to understand fully why`      IS `reasons`
        `says the claimant may apply to the Authority for mediation within 90 days`           IS TRUE
        `says the claimant may go to the Court if mediation does not resolve the dispute`     IS TRUE
        `says a Court application must be lodged within 28 days after the mediator's certificate` IS TRUE
        `says proceedings may be started only after an unsuccessful mediation`                IS TRUE
        `says an interim determination may be sought once mediation is applied for`           IS TRUE
        `was given at the same time as the notice of the dispute`                             IS TRUE
        `came with a copy of the statement and the approved information bulletin on mediation` IS `bulletin`

#ASSERT `the statement meets s 85(8) and (9)` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the statement meets s 85(8) and (9)` (`a dispute statement with` FALSE TRUE))
-- Reg 13 is a separate duty: a statement without the bulletin still meets s 85(8) and (9), and counts for s 87(3)(b).
#ASSERT `the statement meets s 85(8) and (9)` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the employer also met reg 13` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE FALSE))
-- s 89 B: due 8 November 2026. Paid 9 November: 1 week. Paid 15 November (7 days late): 1. Paid 16 November (8 days): 2,
-- the part week counting as a whole. Paid on 8 November: 0.
#ASSERT `B, the weeks late under s 89(1)` (`the calendar date` 8 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 9 11 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `B, the weeks late under s 89(1)` (`the calendar date` 8 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 15 11 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `B, the weeks late under s 89(1)` (`the calendar date` 8 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 16 11 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `B, the weeks late under s 89(1)` (`the calendar date` 8 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 8 11 2026) EQUALS 0

§ `ss 65C, 84(5), 85A, 86, 88 -- penalties and dismissal`

#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `refusing to receive a claim, or dismissing a worker only for claiming (s 84(5))` TRUE EQUALS 85
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `refusing to receive a claim, or dismissing a worker only for claiming (s 84(5))` FALSE EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `not giving earnings information within 21 days without reasonable excuse (s 85A(2))` FALSE EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `not deciding an application to alter weekly payments within 14 days (s 86(2))` TRUE EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `not making a weekly payment in time (s 88(1))` TRUE EQUALS 125
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `dismissing an incapacitated worker within 6 months of the injury (s 65C(1))` FALSE EQUALS 200
-- Injured 1 March 2026; the relevant period ends 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of the s 65C relevant period` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `the dismissal would be an offence under s 65C (up to 200 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `the dismissal would be an offence under s 65C (up to 200 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026) EQUALS `not an offence under s 65C: outside the 6 months after the injury`
#ASSERT `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not an offence under s 65C: the reason is the worker's serious misconduct (s 65C(3))`
#ASSERT `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `not an offence under s 65C: the worker is not incapacitated for work by the injury`

§ `ss 75B, 69, 103D, 104 -- the worker's deadlines`

#ASSERT `weekly compensation may now be reduced or cancelled under ss 75B and 69` TRUE 14 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`weekly compensation may now be reduced or cancelled under ss 75B and 69` TRUE 13 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`weekly compensation may now be reduced or cancelled under ss 75B and 69` FALSE 30 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`weekly compensation may now be reduced or cancelled under ss 75B and 69` TRUE 30 FALSE)
-- Statement received 1 October 2026: mediation by 30 December (90 days). Certificate received 1 October: Court by 29 October.
#ASSERT `the last day to apply for mediation under s 103D(1A)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 12 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to commence proceedings under s 104(3)` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026

§ `Regulative rules`

-- s 80: notice was practicable within 3 days; given on day 2. Not given by day 4: a breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 80(1) -- the worker must give notice of the injury as soon as practicable` 3) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `give notice of the injury` 2)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the worker, "s 80(1): no compensation unless notice of the injury was given ..."
#TRACE `s 80(1) -- the worker must give notice of the injury as soon as practicable` 3 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 4)

-- s 182(1): injured Sunday 1 March 2026, the 6 months end on 1 September 2026, day 184 (31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31). A
-- claim on day 184: met. Not by then: only the s 182(3) saving remains; a claim relying on it on day 200: met.
#ASSERT `days from` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) `to` (`the last day to claim under s 182(1)` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026)) EQUALS 184
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 182(1) -- the worker must make the claim within 6 months` 184) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make the claim` 184)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 182(1) -- the worker must make the claim within 6 months` 184) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 185), (EVENT `the worker` `make the claim, relying on s 182(3)` 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: PARTY the worker MAY make the claim, relying on s 182(3) (the permission still open)
#TRACE `s 182(1) -- the worker must make the claim within 6 months` 184 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 185)

-- s 82(2): the certificate on day 0, the claim form on day 28: in time. On day 29: a breach (the claim is made only then).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 82(2) -- the worker must give the remaining claim document within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `give the remaining claim document` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the worker, "s 82(2): the claim and the medical certificate of capacity were not both given within 28 days ..."
#TRACE `s 82(2) -- the worker must give the remaining claim document within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `give the remaining claim document` AT 29

-- The claim chain. Day 0 is Monday 26 October 2026, when the employer receives a claim for weekly payments. The 3rd
-- working day is Thursday 29 October (day 3), the 10th is Monday 9 November (day 14). For a decision on Thursday
-- 5 November (day 10), the 3rd working day after is Tuesday 10 November, 5 days on. With no decision, acceptance is
-- deemed on Tuesday 10 November (day 15), and the 3rd working day after that is Friday 13 November (day 18), 3 days on.
`the spans for a claim received on Monday 26 October 2026` MEANS
    `Working-day spans` WITH
        `calendar days to the 3rd working day after the claim was received`  IS 3
        `calendar days to the 10th working day after the claim was received` IS 14
        `calendar days to the 3rd working day after the decision`            IS 5
        `calendar days to the 3rd working day after the day acceptance is deemed` IS 3

#ASSERT `days from` (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026) `to` (`the last day to commence weekly payments on a deemed acceptance under s 87(1), on the s 85(2) reading` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) 0 0) EQUALS 3

`the claim rules` MEANS `ss 84(1), 85, 87 -- the employer must forward the claim, decide it in time and pay on acceptance or deferral` TRUE `the spans for a claim received on Monday 26 October 2026`

-- Forwarded day 2, accepted day 10, payments started day 15: every duty met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 2), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `accept liability`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 15)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(2): on accepting a claim for weekly payments, the employer must start them within 3 working days" (started day 16)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 2
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `accept liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 16
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 84(1): the employer must forward the claim ... within 3 working days ..." (forwarded day 4)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 4
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `accept liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 12
-- Deferred day 10, payments day 12, accepted day 60 (inside the 56 days to day 66): met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 12), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `accept liability`) 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Deferred day 10 and disputed properly on day 66, the last day of the deferral: met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 12), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, with the s 85(8) statement`) 66)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(4)(a), 87(2): the deferral ran out after 56 days without a decision ..." (nothing by day 66)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 12
    (WAITUNTIL 67)
-- Deferred day 10, payments day 12, disputed on day 40 without the statement but with it given the same day: met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 12), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement`) 40), (EVENT `the employer` (`give the claimant a dispute statement` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE TRUE)) 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Deferred day 10, disputed day 40 with no statement at all: the dispute ends the deferral (s 85(4)(a)), so no s 87(2)
-- deemed acceptance, but s 85(8) is not met.
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(8), (9): the employer disputed liability without giving, at the same time, the statement ..."
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 12
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement` AT 40
    (WAITUNTIL 41)
-- A second deferral does not end the first: expect the s 85(4)(a), 87(2) breach again.
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 12
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `defer accepting liability` AT 40
    (WAITUNTIL 67)
-- Disputed properly on day 10: nothing more is owed under these rules (the worker's mediation clock starts, s 103D).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, with the s 85(8) statement`) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Disputed on day 10 without the statement (corrected 24 October 2026, finding 18): the dispute is a decision notified
-- within the 10 working days, so liability is not deemed accepted and no weekly payments are owed under s 87. The
-- statement was owed at the same time: given the same day, met; not given, expect the s 85(8) breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` (`give the claimant a dispute statement` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE TRUE)) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(8), (9): the employer disputed liability without giving, at the same time, the statement ..." (none by day 11)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- A statement whose reasons are not detailed enough (s 85(9)) does not meet the duty either.
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(8), (9): ..." (the statement of day 10 does not count)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the decision on liability` `dispute liability, without the s 85(8) statement` AT 10
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `give the claimant a dispute statement` (`a dispute statement with` FALSE TRUE) AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- No decision by day 14: acceptance is deemed on day 15 (Tuesday 10 November), which the trace reaches with a WAITUNTIL,
-- and payments are owed by the 3rd working day after it, Friday 13 November (day 18). Paid day 18: met. Not paid by day
-- 18: a breach, seen at day 19. (Corrected 24 October 2026: the first version allowed 5 days, to day 20.)
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim rules` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (WAITUNTIL 15), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 18)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the s 87 obligation still open: PARTY the employer MUST commence weekly payments WITHIN 3 (started at day 15)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 87(1): no decision was notified within 10 working days, so liability is deemed accepted ..." (nothing paid by day 18)
#TRACE `the claim rules` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the claim` AT 1
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
    (WAITUNTIL 19)
-- A claim for medical costs only (not weekly payments), accepted day 10, paid day 30: met (s 85(3) sets no period).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 84(1), 85, 87 -- the employer must forward the claim, decide it in time and pay on acceptance or deferral` FALSE `the spans for a claim received on Monday 26 October 2026`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `forward the claim` 1), (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the decision on liability` `accept liability`) 10), (EVENT `the employer` `pay the compensation claimed` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 85(8) on its own, from the moment of a notice of dispute (day 10): a statement meeting s 85(8) and (9) the same
-- day: met. One whose reasons are too thin: a breach. None: a breach, seen at day 11.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 85(8) -- with a notice of dispute, the employer must give the claimant the statement in the approved form` 10 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` (`give the claimant a dispute statement` (`a dispute statement with` TRUE FALSE)) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(8), (9): the employer disputed liability without giving, at the same time, the statement ..."
#TRACE `s 85(8) -- with a notice of dispute, the employer must give the claimant the statement in the approved form` AT 10 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `give the claimant a dispute statement` (`a dispute statement with` FALSE TRUE) AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 85(8), (9): ..." (no statement at all)
#TRACE `s 85(8) -- with a notice of dispute, the employer must give the claimant the statement in the approved form` AT 10 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)

-- s 84(5): over 180 days, no refusal and no dismissal: met. A dismissal for claiming on day 20: a breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 84(5) -- the employer must not refuse to receive a claim, or dismiss the worker for claiming` 180) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 181)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 84(5)(b): dismissing a worker only for giving or trying to give a claim is an offence ..."
#TRACE `s 84(5) -- the employer must not refuse to receive a claim, or dismiss the worker for claiming` 180 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `dismiss the worker` AT 20

